data.content:
Your project targets **.NET 10** and has filesystem statics in `ReportGenerator.cs`. The best approach is to adopt the **`System.IO.Abstractions`** NuGet package — it's battle-tested and already wraps `File.*`, `Directory.*`, `Path.*`, etc.

### 1. Install the packages

```bash
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions                    # production code
dotnet add <YourTestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers  # tests
```

### 2. Register in DI (`Program.cs`)

```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

### 3. Inject `IFileSystem` into your classes

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions;

public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var outputDir = Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
        {
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);
        }

        var reportPath = fileSystem.Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}.txt");
        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, $"Report: {reportName}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

The key mapping is:
| Static call | Replacement |
|---|---|
| `File.WriteAllText(…)` | `fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(…)` |
| `File.ReadAllText(…)` | `fileSystem.File.ReadAllText(…)` |
| `Directory.Exists(…)` | `fileSystem.Directory.Exists(…)` |

### 4. Test with `MockFileSystem`

```csharp
using System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers;

var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");

var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs);
var path = generator.GenerateReport("sales");

Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists(path));
Assert.Contains("Report: sales", mockFs.File.ReadAllText(path));
```

**Why this over a custom wrapper?** `System.IO.Abstractions` covers the entire `System.IO` surface, so you won't need to extend your interface every time you use a new `File`/`Directory`/`Path` method. The `MockFileSystem` gives you an in-memory filesystem out of the box — no mocking framework needed.

> **Note:** Your `ReportGenerator` also uses `DateTime.UtcNow`, `Environment.*`, and `Console.*`. If you want those testable too, use `TimeProvider` (built-in on .NET 10) for time, and small custom wrappers for Environment/Console. Let me know if you'd like guidance on those.
